INSERT INTO `question_import_items` VALUES (1,1,NULL,'Under the Philippine Civil Code provisions on Partnership, which of the following acts requires the unanimous consent of all the partners to bind the partnership?','mcq','[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Assigning the partnership property in trust for creditors or on the assignee\'s promise to pay the debts of the partnership.\",\"is_correct\":true},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Entering into a contract of sale for inventory items usually traded by the business.\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"Appointing a managing partner to handle the daily logistical operations of the firm.\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"D\",\"text\":\"Paying off long-term operational liabilities using partnership liquidity. more but less than all the partners have no authority to assign partnership property in trust for creditors or on the assignee\'s promise to pay partnership debts.\",\"is_correct\":false}]','Article 1818 of the Civil Code states that unless authorized by the other partners, one or','moderate','rule',85,'pending',0,'2026-09-08 13:24:19','2026-09-08 13:24:19'),(2,1,NULL,'X, Y, and Z organized a partnership where X and Y are general partners contributing 50,000 Pesos each, and Z is an industrial partner contributing his technical expertise. The firm incurred third-party obligations amounting to 130,000 Pesos. If the partnership assets are exhausted, how much can external creditors collect from Z?','mcq','[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Nothing, because industrial partners are legally exempt from sharing any partnership losses.\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"A pro-rata share of the remaining debt out of his personal assets, though he may demand reimbursement from X and Y.\",\"is_correct\":true},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"One-third of the total debt with no right to seek reimbursement from the general partners.\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"D\",\"text\":\"The entire 130,000 Pesos because industrial partners have unlimited solidary liability in the first instance. all their property for partnership debts after partnership assets have been exhausted. However, under Article 1797, an industrial partner is exempt from losses internally, meaning he can seek reimbursement from the capitalist partners.\",\"is_correct\":false}]','Article 1816 specifies that all partners, including industrial ones, are liable pro-rata with','moderate','rule',85,'pending',1,'2026-09-08 13:24:19','2026-09-08 13:24:19'),(3,1,NULL,'A, B, and C are partners in \'ABC Electronics Trading\'. Without the knowledge of B and C, Partner A purchases a large shipment of counterfeit microchips in the firm\'s name. The shipment is seized, and a third-party client sues the partnership for damages. What is the extent of liability of B and C?','mcq','[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"B and C are completely free from liability because the purchase was unauthorized and fraudulent.\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"B and C are solidarily liable with Partner A and the partnership for the tortious\\/wrongful act.\",\"is_correct\":true},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"B and C are liable only up to their respective capital contributions.\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"D\",\"text\":\"B and C are only criminally liable but free from civil obligations. party by any wrongful act or omission of any partner acting in the ordinary course of business, the partnership and all the partners are liable solidarily.\",\"is_correct\":false}]','Under Articles 1822 and 1823 of the Civil Code, where injury or loss is caused to a third','moderate','rule',85,'pending',2,'2026-09-08 13:24:19','2026-09-08 13:24:19'),(4,1,NULL,'In a contract of partnership, which of the following stipulations is considered completely null and void?','mcq','[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"A stipulation exempting a capitalist partner from any share in the losses.\",\"is_correct\":true},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"A stipulation providing for an unequal distribution of profits despite equal capital inputs.\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"A stipulation giving the managing partner the absolute power to dissolve the firm.\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"D\",\"text\":\"A stipulation granting third-party creditors a share in net profits as interest on a loan. partners from any share in the profits or losses is void. While an industrial partner is exempt from losses by law, a capitalist partner cannot be exempted by mere stipulation.\",\"is_correct\":false}]','Article 1799 explicitly mandates that any stipulation which excludes one or more','moderate','rule',85,'pending',3,'2026-09-08 13:24:19','2026-09-08 13:24:19'),(5,1,NULL,'Which of the following establishes a partnership by estoppel under Philippine jurisprudence?','mcq','[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"A non-partner represents himself, or consents to another representing him to anyone, as a partner in an existing partnership or with other persons.\",\"is_correct\":true},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"A person receives a share of the profits of a business as wages of an employee or rent to a landlord.\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"Joint tenancy or co-ownership of real property where profits are split equally among owners.\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"D\",\"text\":\"Sharing gross returns from property which the individuals hold a joint or common interest in. himself or consents to being represented as a partner, he is liable to any person to whom such representation has been made who has given credit on the faith of it.\",\"is_correct\":false}]','Article 1825 governs partnership by estoppel, stating that when a person represents','moderate','rule',85,'pending',4,'2026-09-08 13:24:19','2026-09-08 13:24:19'),(6,2,NULL,'Under the Philippine Civil Code provisions on Partnership, which of the following acts requires the unanimous consent of all the partners to bind the partnership?','mcq','[{\"la