85,'pending',1,'2026-09-08 13:29:52','2026-09-08 13:29:52'),(13,3,NULL,'A, B, and C are partners in \'ABC Electronics Trading\'. Without the knowledge of B and C, Partner A purchases a large shipment of counterfeit microchips in the firm\'s name. The shipment is seized, and a third-party client sues the partnership for damages. What is the extent of liability of B and C?','mcq','[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"B and C are completely free from liability because the purchase was unauthorized and fraudulent.\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"B and C are solidarily liable with Partner A and the partnership for the tortious\\/wrongful act.\",\"is_correct\":true},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"B and C are liable only up to their respective capital contributions.\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"D\",\"text\":\"B and C are only criminally liable but free from civil obligations. party by any wrongful act or omission of any partner acting in the ordinary course of business, the partnership and all the partners are liable solidarily.\",\"is_correct\":false}]','Under Articles 1822 and 1823 of the Civil Code, where injury or loss is caused to a third','moderate','rule',85,'pending',2,'2026-09-08 13:29:52','2026-09-08 13:29:52'),(14,3,NULL,'In a contract of partnership, which of the following stipulations is considered completely null and void?','mcq','[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"A stipulation exempting a capitalist partner from any share in the losses.\",\"is_correct\":true},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"A stipulation providing for an unequal distribution of profits despite equal capital inputs.\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"A stipulation giving the managing partner the absolute power to dissolve the firm.\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"D\",\"text\":\"A stipulation granting third-party creditors a share in net profits as interest on a loan. partners from any share in the profits or losses is void. While an industrial partner is exempt from losses by law, a capitalist partner cannot be exempted by mere stipulation.\",\"is_correct\":false}]','Article 1799 explicitly mandates that any stipulation which excludes one or more','moderate','rule',85,'pending',3,'2026-09-08 13:29:52','2026-09-08 13:29:52'),(15,3,NULL,'Which of the following establishes a partnership by estoppel under Philippine jurisprudence?','mcq','[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"A non-partner represents himself, or consents to another representing him to anyone, as a partner in an existing partnership or with other persons.\",\"is_correct\":true},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"A person receives a share of the profits of a business as wages of an employee or rent to a landlord.\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"Joint tenancy or co-ownership of real property where profits are split equally among owners.\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"D\",\"text\":\"Sharing gross returns from property which the individuals hold a joint or common interest in. himself or consents to being represented as a partner, he is liable to any person to whom such representation has been made who has given credit on the faith of it.\",\"is_correct\":false}]','Article 1825 governs partnership by estoppel, stating that when a person represents','moderate','rule',85,'pending',4,'2026-09-08 13:29:52','2026-09-08 13:29:52'),(19,6,NULL,'A general partnership is constituted with three partners: A, B, and C, who contributed equal capital. D, a non-partner, allows his name to be included in the firm name, \'A, B, C, and D.\' The partnership subsequently incurs heavy business debts to external creditors. What is the legal status and liability of D regarding these partnership debts?','mcq','[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"D is a partner by estoppel and is liable as a general partner to third-party creditors who relied on the partnership name, even though D has no proprietary interest in the business.\",\"is_correct\":true},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"D is considered an industrial partner and shares equally in the profits and losses of the partnership.\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"D has no liability whatsoever because his consent was obtained without formal documentation filed with the Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC).\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"D\",\"text\":\"D is treated as a limited partner whose liability is strictly limited to the capital contributions he intended to make. allows their name to be included in a firm name\\u2014when they are not an actual partner\\u2014becomes a partner by estoppel. They are liable to third parties who extend credit or rely in good faith upon the representation, as though they were an actual general partner. Subject: Financial Accounting and Reporting (FAR)\",\"is_correct\":false}]','Under the Civil Code provisions governing partnerships in the Philippines, a person who','moderate','rule',85,'pending',0,'2026-09-08 14:03:30','2026-09-08 14:03:30'),(20,6,NULL,'Entity X sells a piece of machinery on January 1, 2026, for P500,000. The buyer pays P100,000 down and signs a 3-year, non-interest-bearing note for P400,000. Market rate of interest for similar notes is 10%. The present value factor of 1 at 10% for 3 periods is 0.7513. At what amount should the note receivable be initially recognized?','mcq','[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"P400,000\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"P300,520\",\"is_correct\":true},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"P500,000\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"D\",\"text\":\"P400,520 Face Value x PV Factor = P400,000 x 0.7513 = P300,520. Subject: Taxation (TAX)\",\"is_correct\":false}]','Non-interest-bearing notes are initially recorded at their present value. Present Value =','moderate','rule',85,'pending',1,'2026-09-08 14:03:30','2026-09-08 14:03:30'),(21,6,NULL,'Under the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC) of the Philippines, as amended, which of the following domestic corporations is subject to a preferential corporate income tax rate, provided specific legal conditions are met?','mcq','[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Proprietary educational institutions and non-profit hospitals.\",\"is_correct\":true},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"General professional partnerships.\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"Publicly listed manufacturing companies.\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"D\",\"text\":\"Regional operating headquarters of multinational companies. preferential tax rate under Section 27(B) of the Tax Code, subject to the limitation that their gross income from unrelated trade, business, or other activity does not exceed 50% of their total gross income.\",\"is_correct\":false}]','Proprietary educational institutions and hospitals which are non-profit are granted a','moderate','rule',85,'pending',2,'2026-09-08 14:03:30','2026-09-08 14:03:30'),(22,7,NULL,'A general partnership is constituted with three partners: A, B, and C, who contributed equal capital. D, a non-partner, allows his name to be included in the firm name, \'A, B, C, and D.\' The partnership subsequently incurs heavy business debts to external creditors. What is the legal status and liability of D regarding these partnership debts?','true_false','[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"True\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"False\",\"is_correct\":true}]','Under Article 1815 and Article 1825 of the Civil Code of the Philippines, a person who allows their name to be included in a firm name, despite not being an actual partner, becomes a partner by estoppel. They are liable to third parties who extend credit or rely in good faith upon the representation, as though they were an actual general partner.','moderate','rule',90,'pending',0,'2026-09-08 14:06:47','2026-09-08 14:06:47'),(23,7,NULL,'On January 1, 2026, an entity purchased equipment for PHP 1,200,000 with an estimated useful life of 5 years and a residual value of PHP 200,000. The entity uses the double-declining balance method of depreciation. What is the depreciation expense for the year ended December 31, 2027 (the second year)?','true_false','[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"True\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"False\",\"is_correct\":true}]','Under the double-declining balance method, the rate is 40% (2 / 5 years). Year 1 Depreciation = PHP 1,200,000 * 40% = PHP 480,000. Book Value at end of Year 1 = PHP 1,200,000 - PHP 480,000 = PHP 720,000. Year 2 Depreciation = PHP 720,000 * 40% = PHP 288,000.','moderate','rule',90,'pending',1,'2026-09-08 14:06:47','2026-09-08 14:06:47'),(24,7,NULL,'Under the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC) of the Philippines, as amended, which of the following is considered a non-taxable de minimis benefit when granted by an employer to an employee?','true_false','[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"True\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"False\",\"is_correct\":true}]','Pursuant to RR No. 11-2018 and existing tax regulations, monetized unused vacation leave credits of private employees not exceeding 10 days during the year is a tax-exempt de minimis benefit.','moderate','rule',90,'pending',2,'2026-09-08 14:06:47','2026-09-08 14:06:47'),(25,7,NULL,'A manufacturing company sells a single product for PHP 150 per unit. The variable cost per unit is PHP 90, and the total fixed costs are PHP 360,000 per year. How many units must the company sell to reach its break-even point?','true_false','[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"True\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"False\",\"is_correct\":true}]','Break-Even Point (Units) = Total Fixed Costs / Contribution Margin per Unit. Contribution Margin per Unit = PHP 150 - PHP 90 = PHP 60. Break-Even Point = PHP 360,000 / PHP 60 = 6,000 units.','moderate','rule',90,'pending',3,'2026-09-08 14:06:47','2026-09-08 14:06:47'),(26,7,NULL,'According to Philippine Standard on Auditing (PSA) 230 (Audit Documentation), what is the standard assembly period for the auditor to complete the administrative process of assembling the final audit file after the date of the auditor\'s report?','true_false','[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"True\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"False\",\"is_correct\":true}]','PSA 230 states that an appropriate time limit within which to complete the assembly of the final audit file is ordinarily not more than 60 days after the date of the auditor\'s report.','moderate','rule',90,'pending',4,'2026-09-08 14:06:47','2026-09-08 14:06:47'),(27,10,NULL,'Which financial statement shows a company\'s financial position at a point in time?','mcq','[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Income Statement\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Statement of Cash Flows\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"Balance Sheet\",\"is_correct\":true},{\"label\":\"D\",\"text\":\"Statement of Changes in Equity\",\"is_correct\":false}]','The Balance Sheet reports assets, liabilities, and equity as of a specific date.','moderate','rule',85,'pending',0,'2026-09-08 14:15:13','2026-09-08 14:15:13'),(28,10,NULL,'Using FIFO during a period of rising prices, which statement is TRUE?','mcq','[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Ending inventory is understated\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Cost of goods sold is higher than under LIFO\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"Ending inventory reflects the most recent (higher) costs\",\"is_correct\":true},{\"label\":\"D\",\"text\":\"Net income is lower than under LIFO income higher than under LIFO.\",\"is_correct\":false}]','FIFO leaves the most recently purchased (higher-cost) units in ending inventory, which also makes reported net','moderate','rule',85,'pending',1,'2026-09-08 14:15:13','2026-09-08 14:15:13'),(29,10,NULL,'Cash is classified as a current asset.','mcq','[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"True\",\"is_correct\":true},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"False\",\"is_correct\":false}]','Cash is always current since it is already in its most liquid form.','moderate','rule',85,'pending',2,'2026-09-08 14:15:13','2026-09-08 14:15:13'),(30,11,NULL,'Which financial statement shows a company\'s financial position at a point in time?','mcq','[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Income Statement\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Statement of Cash Flows\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"Balance Sheet\",\"is_correct\":true},{\"label\":\"D\",\"text\":\"Statement of Changes in Equity\",\"is_correct\":false}]','The Balance Sheet reports assets, liabilities, and equity as of a specific date.','easy','rule',90,'pending',0,'2026-09-08 14:17:12','2026-09-08 14:17:12'),(31,11,NULL,'Using FIFO during a period of rising prices, which statement is TRUE?','mcq','[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Ending inventory is understated\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Cost of goods sold is higher than under LIFO\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"Ending inventory reflects the most recent (higher) costs\",\"is_correct\":true},{\"label\":\"D\",\"text\":\"Net income is lower than under LIFO\",\"is_correct\":false}]','FIFO leaves the most recently purchased (higher-cost) units in ending inventory, which also makes reported net income higher than under LIFO.','moderate','rule',90,'pending',1,'2026-09-08 14:17:12','2026-09-08 14:17:12'),(32,11,NULL,'Cash is classified as a current asset.','mcq','[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"True\",\"is_correct\":true},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"False\",\"is_correct\":false}]','Cash is always current since it is already in its most liquid form.','easy','rule',90,'pending',2,'2026-09-08 14:17:12','2026-09-08 14:17:12'),(33,12,NULL,'Which financial statement shows a company\'s financial position at a point in time?','mcq','[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Income Statement\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Statement of Cash Flows\",\"is_correct\":false},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"Balance Sheet\",\"is_correct\":true},{\"label\":\"D\",\"text\":\"Statement of Changes in Equity\